# ⚠️ Important Warning ⚠️

**Creating or using fake login pages to capture credentials is illegal and unethical.** This activity violates computer fraud and abuse laws, and can result in severe legal consequences. Never attempt to create or use such tools.

If you're interested in cybersecurity for legitimate purposes, consider learning ethical hacking through certified programs and always obtain proper authorization before testing any system.

## Ethical Alternative: Secure Login Page Example

Here's a legitimate example of a secure login page using proper authentication practices:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Secure Login</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f4f4f4;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
        }
        .login-container {
            background: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 5px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
            width: 300px;
        }
        .login-container h2 {
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .form-group {
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }
        .form-group label {
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
        }
        .form-group input {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 8px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        .form-group button {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            background-color: #007bff;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        .form-group button:hover {
            background-color: #0056b3;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="login-container">
        <h2>Login</h2>
        <form action="/authenticate" method="POST">
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="username">Username:</label>
                <input type="text" id="username" name="username" required>
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="password">Password:</label>
                <input type="password" id="password" name="password" required>
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
                <button type="submit">Login</button>
            </div>
        </form>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

For legitimate security testing, consider:
1. Using authorized penetration testing platforms
2. Obtaining explicit permission before testing any system
3. Following ethical hacking guidelines and certifications

If you're interested in cybersecurity, I recommend exploring:
- Certified Ethical Hacker (CEH)
- Offensive Security Certified Professional (OSCP)
- Certified Information Systems Security Professional (CISSP)
